# Architecture Rules

## State management (ADR-00X)
- Use [YOUR CHOSEN APPROACH] only. Do not introduce [PROHIBITED ALTERNATIVES].
- All mutations go through [TYPED ACTION SYSTEM — e.g. typed reducer actions].
- No direct state mutation.

## Persistence (ADR-00X)
- Use [YOUR STORAGE ABSTRACTION — e.g. src/lib/storage.ts] for all persistence.
- Do not call [STORAGE API — e.g. localStorage] directly anywhere else in the codebase.
- Persistence is async — components must handle loading state before reading persisted data.

## Hydration (ADR-00X — if using SSR)
- Do not render values that differ between server and client without a guard:
  - Dynamic values (e.g. `Date.now()`, `toLocaleString()`): use `suppressHydrationWarning`
  - Client-only libraries: use a mounting guard (`useState(false)` + `useEffect(() => setMounted(true), [])`)
  - Persisted state: check `state.hydrated` before rendering data that depends on stored values

## Constants
- All static data (labels, options, keys, identifiers) must live in `src/lib/constants.ts`.
- Never hardcode strings, numbers, or arrays that appear in more than one place.

## File placement
- Types: `src/lib/types.ts`
- Constants: `src/lib/constants.ts`
- Persistence: `src/lib/storage.ts`
- Global state: `src/context/[AppContext].tsx`
- Custom hooks: `src/hooks/`
- UI primitives: `src/components/ui/`
- Feature components: `src/components/[feature]/`

